# Condition checker cron line (Ref #346 PR 5).
#
# NOT INSTALLED. Install only with Bucket's approval: the checker runs every
# 5 minutes, reads pm2/Supabase/disk and writes to the shared JSONL error
# log, so it should not appear on the VPS without a decision.
#
# Log-only condition checks: no published narrative > 2h, no editor draft
# > 3h, > 5 app restarts in 15 min, 3 consecutive failed Supabase health
# probes, missing Supabase env (config_missing), disk used > 80%. Breaches
# land in ~/myboon-logs/errors.jsonl (kinds publish_stale / draft_stale /
# restart_burst / supabase_health_failed / config_missing / disk_high);
# stopped PM2 apps keep their staleness checks silent.
*/5 * * * * cd /home/ubuntu/myboon && pnpm --filter @myboon/collectors pipeline-store:check >> /home/ubuntu/myboon-logs/condition-check.cron.log 2>&1

# Lane-store prune cron line (Ref #346 PR 6).
#
# NOT INSTALLED. Install only with Bucket's approval, and only AFTER the
# #377 managed-entity backfill has completed and the same command has been run
# as a dry run (no --apply) with its JSON reviewed: this prune deletes old
# terminal rows from the two lane SQLite stores (news-lane.sqlite /
# polymarket-lane.sqlite). 14-day retention for terminal run / observation /
# research rows, 7-day retention for delivered outbox rows; pipeline_watchlist,
# undelivered outbox rows, non-terminal rows and failed / dead-letter rows are
# never deleted. Statuses and safety rules:
# packages/collectors/src/lane-store/prune.ts. A lane whose file is missing is
# skipped, never created.
35 4 * * * cd /home/ubuntu/myboon && pnpm --filter @myboon/collectors lane-store:prune -- --apply >> /home/ubuntu/myboon-logs/lane-store-prune.cron.log 2>&1